+// 1377/1380 hello + 3213/3216 prog functions and ours' on 1377/1380 + 3211/
+// 3216; the only refs present in the code but absent from a side's self_pp are
+// 2, both ours, both of kind (size=3, V=1).
+//
+// => The shortfall is a defect of THIS FILE'S DECODER, in the pool branch
+// of ComputeShorebirdCodeFacts at :1350-1383 (:1318-1331 before this block
+// grew), not a codegen gap. The pool form is charged a fixed three words there
+// (`int32_t ahead = 3 - used;` then `i += 1 + ahead`), so a decoded pool load
+// swallows the two words behind it. Counting refs that fall within 2 words of
+// the previous ref gives prog OURS 2, prog THEIRS 0, hello both 0 -- exactly
+// the two that go missing. Their layout has NOPs at that site; our tighter
+// codegen does not, so the fixed skip eats a genuine reference. The 44
+// subgraph_pp slots are the same two depth-0 slots propagated to 44 callers.
+//
+// CAVEAT, keep it: their analyzer may carry the same three-word skip and
+// simply never be triggered by their own layout. That is not directly testable
+// -- the snapshot version hash makes their analyze_snapshot refuse our .so and
+// ours refuse theirs ("Wrong full snapshot version, expected '8b59e404...'
+// found '839937dd...'", rc=255).
+//
+// Also retracted: "we do emit index 1332 elsewhere (hello 2x, prog 1x)", which
